content:
{
 "queue": "hr",
 "summary": "Employee E028 Aisha Bello (Payroll Specialist, Finance) asks whether Fernhollow pays for jury duty or whether she must use PTO for a jury summons covering the week of Jan 11 (2027), and whether she needs to send the summons to anyone. I checked POL-PTO-01 (Paid time off); it covers accrual, carry-over, booking and notice only and says nothing about jury duty. No policy I checked covers jury duty. Please advise on pay treatment and any notification steps."
}

{
 "kind": "escalated",
 "message": "Hi Aisha, I couldn't find a policy that covers jury duty. The PTO policy (POL-PTO-01) covers accrual, carry-over and booking, but doesn't say whether jury duty is paid or whether it counts as PTO, and it doesn't mention whom to notify. I've passed your question to the HR team, who can confirm how jury duty is handled and whether you need to send the summons to anyone. They'll reply to you directly. Please keep the summons handy for them.",
 "cited_policy_ids": [
  "POL-PTO-01"
 ]
}
